Q: How to animate line clamp A: <p>Solution using css custom properties and lh units. Hope it helps. The limitation is the expected max lines of the expanded content.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>@property --tip-clamp {
    syntax: '&lt;integer&gt;';
    inherits: true;
    initial-value: 3;
}

.tip-message {
    --tip-clamp: 3;
    --tip-transition: 1.2s;
    display: block;
    max-height: calc(var(--tip-clamp) * 1lh);
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: max-height var(--tip-transition) ease-in-out;
    max-width: 300px;
    margin-top: auto;
}

.tip-message:hover {
    --tip-clamp: 15;
}

.tip-message&gt;span {
    display: -webkit-box;
    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    -webkit-line-clamp: var(--tip-clamp);
    line-clamp: var(--tip-clamp);
    transition: --tip-clamp 0s ease var(--tip-transition);
}

.tip-message:hover&gt;span {
    transition: --tip-clamp 0s;
}</code></pre>
