Q: jquery selector to find a child element with A: <p>Since <code>this</code> is pointing to the <code>span</code> element which is the sibling of the parent of <code>label</code>, <code>$(this).find('.nodeCheckIcon:first')</code> is not going to work. I dont know about your complete markup structure, but if you have a wrapping container for this span element then you can try this</p>

<pre><code>$(this).parent().find('.nodeCheckIcon:first');
</code></pre>
